  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">iDEFEAT TB - Institutional Strengthening to Accelerate Actions for TB and Drug-Resistant TB in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(India):  ..The overall goal of the project is to strengthen TB-related.institutions, focusing on programmatic and clinical management of patients with.TB and drug-resistant TB (DR-TB). These goals are the achievement of the.National Strategic Plan and United Nations High Level Meeting TB targets for.India. .. ..With FY 2022 funds, USAID/India will.contribute to the following objectives: (1) provide institutional strengthening.of DR-TB care facilities through centers of excellence that support the.National TB Elimination Program&apos;s (NTEP) patient-centered and quality.assured DR-TB care endeavors; (2) strengthen TB institutions to support the.NTEP &apos;s efforts to improve the programmatic and clinical management of TB and.DR-TB, pediatric TB, extra pulmonary TB (EPTB), latent TB, and TB preventive.therapy; (3) develop and scale-up digital and blended learning approaches to.rapidly build the TB care and management capacity of NTEP staff; (4).improve the quality of TB care and program management by engaging District TB.program managers through a continuous quality improvement approach; and (5).invigorate the corporate sector mobilization for India&apos;s TB response. .. ..This intervention supports the U.S. Government&apos;s Global.Tuberculosis Strategy, which aims to reach every person with TB, cure those in.need of treatment, and prevent the spread of disease and new infections. It.also contributes to the USAID Global Accelerator to End Tuberculosis, USAID&apos;s.contribution to the UN target of treating 40 million people between 2018 and.2022. ..</narrative>
  </description>
